WEBVTT

00:42.542 --> 00:45.962
SOLD OUT ON YOU

00:46.546 --> 00:48.256
Mr. Mechoori.

00:49.674 --> 00:50.925
What took you so long?

00:52.302 --> 00:53.762
I told you I'd be home late.

00:54.387 --> 00:56.181
Why were you sleeping here?

00:56.264 --> 00:57.265
Did you take your meds?

00:57.348 --> 00:58.558
You only took one pack, right?

00:58.641 --> 01:00.143
Did you have dinner…

01:19.954 --> 01:21.456
I missed you.

02:42.287 --> 02:43.788
CAUTION
MAY CAUSE DIZZINESS

03:20.992 --> 03:22.493
Mr. Mechoori.

03:25.330 --> 03:26.331
Yes?

03:28.666 --> 03:29.667
Did you sleep well?

03:29.751 --> 03:31.711
Yes, I did.

03:33.463 --> 03:36.424
You didn't look comfortable
sleeping on the sofa last night,

03:36.507 --> 03:38.092
so I moved you to your room.

03:40.053 --> 03:41.095
Right.

03:41.179 --> 03:42.847
-Thank you.
-Sure.

03:45.058 --> 03:46.726
You look a bit tired today.

03:46.809 --> 03:48.269
Should I go run by myself?

03:48.353 --> 03:50.355
No, it's fine. You can warm up first.

03:53.775 --> 03:54.651
I'll be out soon.

03:57.737 --> 03:58.988
Okay.

04:02.825 --> 04:05.286
Mr. Mechoori, could you slow…

04:08.081 --> 04:09.082
Wait.

04:10.208 --> 04:12.126
Hey, I said slow down a little.

04:12.210 --> 04:13.461
What are you doing?

04:16.506 --> 04:17.924
What?

04:18.508 --> 04:20.718
DEOKPUNG VILLAGE

04:21.594 --> 04:23.179
Hey, Changsik!

04:23.263 --> 04:26.683
Hey, how could you just run off
without Changsik?

04:26.766 --> 04:29.227
He was desperately looking for you.

04:29.310 --> 04:31.312
Right, Changsik?

04:31.396 --> 04:32.814
You missed him, didn't you?

04:32.897 --> 04:34.190
I missed you.

04:38.695 --> 04:40.571
Aren't you going to stretch?

04:40.655 --> 04:42.031
Well…

04:42.115 --> 04:42.991
Come on, Changsik.

04:43.992 --> 04:45.410
I was just about to.

04:45.493 --> 04:46.703
Stay here.

04:46.786 --> 04:47.912
What's his deal?

04:49.664 --> 04:52.500
Mr. Mechoori, how about getting a TV?

04:52.583 --> 04:53.960
I'll buy it for you.

04:54.043 --> 04:56.170
There's nothing to do, so I'm just bored.

04:56.254 --> 04:59.257
I want to catch up
on some TV shows and movies.

04:59.340 --> 05:00.425
And I miss variety shows.

05:00.508 --> 05:01.509
I missed you.

05:12.729 --> 05:13.771
Are you all right?

05:18.609 --> 05:19.610
Gosh, it's so hot.

05:19.694 --> 05:22.447
It's hot even in the morning.

05:22.530 --> 05:25.658
I heard there's a place where the weather
is like spring all-year round.

05:25.742 --> 05:28.453
Where was it? Somewhere in Colombia…

05:29.537 --> 05:30.788
Bogotá!

05:33.374 --> 05:35.335
-Bogotá!
-I missed you.

05:39.589 --> 05:40.423
What are you doing?

05:44.469 --> 05:46.012
Let's continue.

05:49.015 --> 05:53.478
I've always wanted to see the sunset
from a lookout in Bogotá.

05:53.561 --> 05:56.105
Why do you have
so many things you want to see?

05:56.189 --> 05:57.815
Finish your stretching and come home.

05:58.983 --> 06:00.193
Let's go, Changsik!

06:06.324 --> 06:07.492
Let's go!

06:25.384 --> 06:26.719
Are you making bean sprout soup?

06:28.221 --> 06:29.388
What's wrong?

06:29.472 --> 06:30.848
-About what?
-What is it?

06:30.932 --> 06:31.766
Bean sprouts.

06:32.350 --> 06:33.851
-What?
-What?

06:47.907 --> 06:50.451
Na Som-yi!
Are you taking money from Mechoori again?

06:55.581 --> 06:57.041
Hey, Jin-yi.

06:57.125 --> 06:58.167
What is it?

07:00.044 --> 07:01.045
Didn't Som-yi come here?

07:02.004 --> 07:03.131
No, she didn't.

07:07.426 --> 07:08.928
Hey, where are you?

07:09.011 --> 07:11.722
School, my foot. Your teacher called
and said you weren't there!

07:11.806 --> 07:14.225
Are you crawling your way there?
You better move it!

07:17.812 --> 07:19.313
She's just about there now.

07:20.648 --> 07:22.316
But what were you doing?

07:27.947 --> 07:30.533
We were going to have breakfast.

07:31.784 --> 07:33.119
I haven't had breakfast either.

07:33.703 --> 07:34.579
Can I join you?

07:42.378 --> 07:45.506
Chili peppers are a must
in bean sprout soup.

07:45.590 --> 07:47.550
Isn't it spicy?
You can't handle spicy food.

07:48.134 --> 07:50.761
-You can't eat spicy food?
-He doesn't like spicy food.

07:53.055 --> 07:54.140
Thanks.

07:58.728 --> 08:00.104
What was that with Som-yi earlier?

08:00.188 --> 08:01.856
She was late to school again.

08:01.939 --> 08:04.317
Her homeroom teacher
probably thinks I'm neglecting her.

08:04.400 --> 08:06.527
Should I have a talk with Som-yi?

08:06.611 --> 08:08.362
As if she'd listen to you.

08:08.905 --> 08:10.907
Still, she seemed interested
in school these days.

08:10.990 --> 08:13.075
She wondered what they'd do
for creative activities.

08:13.159 --> 08:15.119
It's because they don't study
during that period.

08:15.203 --> 08:17.288
I have no idea
what's going to become of her.

08:17.371 --> 08:19.582
I think she's good with her hands.

08:20.416 --> 08:23.336
Last time, she won
the 3D-pen crafting contest.

08:24.337 --> 08:27.048
Did you forget
how she kept begging you for a 3D pen

08:27.131 --> 08:29.342
but quit two days after buying it for her?

08:36.807 --> 08:38.059
Don't eat so fast.

09:04.168 --> 09:06.295
You think you can just run away
and hide in here?

09:06.379 --> 09:09.715
Come out and see for yourself
what you've done!

09:09.799 --> 09:12.802
I'll make sure it's in your face
every moment of every day.

09:13.469 --> 09:15.012
Come out.

09:15.096 --> 09:17.223
Come out here!

09:17.306 --> 09:20.351
Come out here right now!

09:27.358 --> 09:28.484
What are you doing?

09:30.695 --> 09:32.863
I'm just trying to digest. What?

09:46.544 --> 09:48.588
Yes, of course. Yes, Ms. Michelle.

09:48.671 --> 09:51.507
I'm on my way to pick him up.

09:52.091 --> 09:53.301
It's a 4:00 p.m. flight.

09:53.384 --> 09:54.677
Yes, ma'am. Goodbye.

10:08.274 --> 10:11.527
You've done a great job
of managing such a busy schedule.

10:12.403 --> 10:13.613
We've only just begun.

10:14.405 --> 10:18.326
I'll become much busier if we're to launch
other L'Étoile product lines.

10:18.409 --> 10:19.452
In Korea?

10:19.535 --> 10:20.828
Yes.

10:21.662 --> 10:23.789
Your flight's in two hours, Mr. Seo.

10:24.332 --> 10:26.000
I'm not going to France.

10:26.083 --> 10:27.752
I threw away that ticket a long time ago.

10:29.545 --> 10:30.838
Then, what about this suitcase?

10:30.921 --> 10:33.382
The vinyl records
that Michelle sent me are in there.

10:33.466 --> 10:36.135
I probably won't have time
to listen to them in Korea now,

10:36.218 --> 10:37.303
so send them back.

10:38.346 --> 10:40.389
Where are you going?

10:40.973 --> 10:41.807
HIT.

10:42.850 --> 10:46.312
Sir, Ms. Michelle
is not going to let this slide.

10:46.395 --> 10:49.774
You could risk your position
by recklessly pushing ahead with this.

10:49.857 --> 10:50.775
I know.

10:50.858 --> 10:53.736
That's why I'm going alone.

11:02.495 --> 11:06.165
We're currently working on the schedule
for La Fin Essence's follow-up broadcast.

11:06.957 --> 11:10.336
We've also requested QA tests
from domestic and international labs,

11:10.419 --> 11:12.546
and we're waiting for the results.

11:14.090 --> 11:16.634
Would you be able to proceed
with this right away?

11:20.388 --> 11:22.139
L'ÉTOILE LUMIÈRE EYE CREAM
PRODUCT INTRO

11:26.018 --> 11:29.230
I'm sure there are conditions
attached to this kind of proposal.

11:29.313 --> 11:30.189
What are they?

11:30.272 --> 11:32.650
Reinstate Ms. Dam Ye-jin.

11:32.733 --> 11:33.901
That's the only condition.

11:33.984 --> 11:36.946
Aren't you aware
of Dam Ye-jin's situation at the moment?

11:37.029 --> 11:39.365
That's why I'm telling you this.

11:39.448 --> 11:42.701
L'Étoile will not work with HIT
unless it's with Ms. Dam.

11:43.285 --> 11:47.706
Where young souls breathed their last

11:47.790 --> 11:49.834
Jeon Jung-muk, I can't hear you!

11:49.917 --> 11:52.461
The wounded old pine trees…

11:54.755 --> 11:58.050
-Mechoori!
-Mechoori!

11:58.134 --> 11:59.802
-Mechoori!
-Let's go out!

11:59.885 --> 12:01.303
-Mechoori!
-Mechoori!

12:01.387 --> 12:02.721
-Mechoori!
-Mechoori, come on out!

12:02.805 --> 12:05.850
-Mechoori!
-Come on out!

12:05.933 --> 12:07.768
-Come on out!
-Let's go running together!

12:07.852 --> 12:10.479
-Come on out!
-Let's go! Gosh.

12:10.563 --> 12:12.106
-Come on!
-Let's go!

12:12.189 --> 12:13.357
Two, three!

12:13.441 --> 12:15.192
To the snow-covered front lines…

12:15.276 --> 12:16.819
Shouldn't you join them?

12:17.611 --> 12:20.656
Let's skip our morning exercise today.
We have to be somewhere.

12:22.575 --> 12:24.493
What is it?

12:24.577 --> 12:26.495
DEOKPUNG VILLAGE
COMMUNITY FESTIVAL

12:27.371 --> 12:28.747
Hey, Mechoori.

12:28.831 --> 12:31.876
So you're not going to be
joining us this time either?

12:31.959 --> 12:32.960
No.

12:33.043 --> 12:36.088
After helping us prepare for the festival,

12:36.172 --> 12:38.048
won't it upset you

12:38.132 --> 12:39.592
-if you don't take part?
-Yeah.

12:39.675 --> 12:40.801
Nope.

12:42.595 --> 12:44.305
Come on, man.

12:44.388 --> 12:46.307
Can't you just help us out tomorrow?

12:46.390 --> 12:48.601
Let's beat Deokpung Village 2 for once!

12:48.684 --> 12:50.769
Having me there won't change the results.

12:50.853 --> 12:52.730
We don't know that for sure.

12:52.813 --> 12:57.151
Mechoori, if you appear
as our village mascot

12:57.234 --> 13:01.155
and rattle them from the start,
we might actually win.

13:01.238 --> 13:03.115
I can't leave my farm unattended.

13:03.782 --> 13:05.743
Well, what did you expect him to say?

13:05.826 --> 13:07.870
Mechoori, I'll throw myself off from here.

13:07.953 --> 13:10.206
-I'm going to fall!
-Okay.

13:13.876 --> 13:14.919
This is scary.

13:17.922 --> 13:23.219
LET'S LIVE TOGETHER IN HARMONY

13:34.146 --> 13:36.690
If you tie it like that,
the wind will loosen it in no time.

13:38.901 --> 13:39.902
Right.

13:41.904 --> 13:43.572
Are you coming to the festival tomorrow?

13:44.240 --> 13:46.492
Yes. I have nothing else to do anyway.

13:46.575 --> 13:48.244
I'm unemployed right now.

13:51.330 --> 13:53.082
How long will you be unemployed for?

13:54.833 --> 13:55.668
Sorry?

13:55.751 --> 13:59.547
I don't know what happened between you two
for Mechoori to act this way,

13:59.630 --> 14:03.467
but everything he's doing for you
is only because he feels responsible.

14:05.052 --> 14:06.053
What does that…

14:06.136 --> 14:08.722
He's managing the farm
and the raw material company.

14:13.435 --> 14:16.522
He always has this strong sense
of responsibility.

14:17.356 --> 14:19.108
So don't lean on him so much.

14:32.204 --> 14:33.455
Responsibility?

14:34.623 --> 14:35.666
All right.

14:35.749 --> 14:37.585
Hey, what's that?

14:39.044 --> 14:41.171
-Look at that car.
-Who's that?

14:41.255 --> 14:43.299
It looks so fancy.

14:59.148 --> 15:00.983
Hey, Mr. Lee.

15:08.908 --> 15:09.742
Mr. Park.

15:10.451 --> 15:11.452
Hello!

15:11.535 --> 15:13.078
How are the preparations going?

15:13.162 --> 15:16.916
Yes! Well, thanks to you,
everything's going great.

15:16.999 --> 15:21.170
I've prepared
a brand new karaoke machine for you.

15:21.253 --> 15:22.671
Make some noise!

15:22.755 --> 15:24.548
Yeah!

15:25.424 --> 15:27.635
-What?
-Yeah!

15:31.931 --> 15:33.474
-I have a strong voice.
-Be careful.

15:33.557 --> 15:35.059
You shouldn't just…

15:41.941 --> 15:43.984
Hey, isn't that Dam Ye-jin?

15:44.068 --> 15:46.487
What is she doing here? What's going on?

15:46.570 --> 15:47.446
I'll tell you later.

15:49.198 --> 15:50.991
You'd better.

15:53.535 --> 15:55.496
-Mr. Park.
-Yes?

15:55.579 --> 15:59.166
Is there a coffee shop nearby
that uses high-quality beans?

15:59.750 --> 16:02.753
Everyone's been working so hard.
I'll go get some drinks for them.

16:04.129 --> 16:05.047
There aren't any.

16:05.798 --> 16:07.841
-I'm sure I heard there was one.
-It's closed.

16:07.925 --> 16:09.843
Right. It was Moon Cafe.

16:10.970 --> 16:12.680
It's probably closed right now.

16:12.763 --> 16:14.598
I'll go and see.

16:17.726 --> 16:18.811
Hey, Ae-ra.

16:23.190 --> 16:24.024
Moon Ae-ra!

16:25.734 --> 16:27.194
Is she out making a delivery?

16:27.277 --> 16:29.613
-She must be away at the moment.
-Well…

16:30.489 --> 16:32.199
Do you always talk like that?

16:33.367 --> 16:34.994
Wait here for a moment.

16:38.205 --> 16:39.123
Moon Ae-ra!

16:48.507 --> 16:50.134
Excuse me…

17:14.199 --> 17:17.411
Where did she go with the shop open?

17:28.672 --> 17:30.174
Moon Ae-ra!

17:31.800 --> 17:34.094
Geez, you scared me.

17:34.178 --> 17:35.471
What is it?

17:36.096 --> 17:36.930
What?

17:37.514 --> 17:39.558
Someone's here to order!
It's a group order!

17:41.977 --> 17:42.811
Excuse me.

17:44.438 --> 17:46.023
It's nice to see you again, Ms. Moon.

17:47.066 --> 17:49.526
I'd like ten cups of coffee
that the village elders like,

17:49.610 --> 17:51.570
and one cappuccino to go.

17:52.571 --> 17:54.448
Read the menu.

17:54.531 --> 17:56.033
I don't sell cappuccinos.

17:56.116 --> 17:57.534
I'm sorry.

17:57.618 --> 18:00.913
I smelled cinnamon in here,
so I thought it was on the menu.

18:02.956 --> 18:05.334
Where on earth is that scent coming from?

18:05.417 --> 18:06.835
Is he a dog or what?

18:10.047 --> 18:11.590
Those look like cappuccinos.

18:12.174 --> 18:14.176
I was just practicing.

18:14.259 --> 18:16.637
The foam's still too airy
for me to sell them.

18:16.720 --> 18:18.180
No, it's perfect.

18:20.182 --> 18:21.016
It looks nice.

18:21.100 --> 18:23.435
The milk foam still looks glossy
even though it's cooled.

18:23.519 --> 18:25.687
It must've been really tasty
when it was freshly made.

18:25.771 --> 18:26.814
Acting like you know…

18:26.897 --> 18:28.690
You get that soft sepia color

18:28.774 --> 18:31.276
only when silky foam
is layered over espresso

18:31.902 --> 18:33.195
with a golden crema.

18:33.278 --> 18:34.738
That's bound to be delicious.

18:35.322 --> 18:37.116
I'm getting curious about the taste.

18:37.783 --> 18:40.369
-Please excuse me.
-I don't sell coffee that's cooled.

18:45.124 --> 18:47.292
Wait just a moment then.

18:47.376 --> 18:50.254
You'll make a cappuccino for me?

18:50.337 --> 18:51.922
I charge double the price
for Seoulites.

18:53.006 --> 18:54.341
But if that's okay…

18:54.925 --> 18:56.260
Double the price.

18:56.343 --> 18:58.095
Thank you very much.

19:38.302 --> 19:39.219
What?

19:40.512 --> 19:42.014
You two are living together?

19:42.890 --> 19:44.057
It just ended up that way.

19:44.141 --> 19:45.726
Hey, you said last time

19:45.809 --> 19:47.978
that you didn't have any feelings for her.

19:48.896 --> 19:49.855
It's not like that.

19:49.938 --> 19:52.900
Don't be silly. You of all people?

19:52.983 --> 19:54.985
Letting someone you don't like
live in your house?

19:55.777 --> 19:57.738
But I don't get Ms. Dam either.

19:57.821 --> 19:59.781
She canceled the show
after you told her to,

19:59.865 --> 20:01.783
and even followed you here.

20:03.452 --> 20:04.620
No way…

20:05.412 --> 20:07.289
Does she still want the raw materials?

20:08.707 --> 20:10.417
I can't accept that.

20:12.085 --> 20:14.546
Aren't you busy? Just go already.

20:16.048 --> 20:18.342
-Bye.
-Okay, bye.

20:20.135 --> 20:20.969
That rascal…

20:27.184 --> 20:28.560
You're pretty late.

20:29.353 --> 20:30.187
I'm sorry.

20:30.979 --> 20:32.522
Did you and Jin-yi…

20:35.150 --> 20:37.569
Never mind. I made dinner. Sit down.

20:38.987 --> 20:40.030
Dinner?

20:59.549 --> 21:01.009
Don't eat it yet.

21:01.593 --> 21:02.594
Well…

21:03.387 --> 21:04.972
This is the highlight. Hang on.

21:10.269 --> 21:12.896
It's supposed to be a smiley face…

21:14.022 --> 21:16.942
I tried making this
since you can't eat any spicy food.

21:22.114 --> 21:25.575
-If it looks bad, I'll eat it.
-No, it smells good.

21:41.717 --> 21:43.343
Did you bite into a shell?

21:50.726 --> 21:52.269
Just spit it out.

21:54.896 --> 21:56.023
It tastes fine.

21:57.190 --> 21:58.650
I'm sorry.

21:58.734 --> 22:00.319
I'll just throw this away.

22:00.402 --> 22:01.820
It's okay.

22:05.073 --> 22:07.576
Mr. Mechoori, are you okay?

22:07.659 --> 22:09.453
Yes, I'm fine.

22:10.412 --> 22:12.789
You know, you're actually pretty clumsy.

22:12.873 --> 22:14.541
Why do you keep bumping into things?

22:14.624 --> 22:17.127
"Keep"? When did I ever
bump into things before?

22:17.210 --> 22:18.295
You bumped into the table

22:18.378 --> 22:20.589
and into the door last time.

22:20.672 --> 22:22.049
You hit it really hard.

22:36.229 --> 22:39.941
THE TRUTH BEHIND THE KISS

22:43.070 --> 22:44.446
He said he'd be really late…

22:46.073 --> 22:47.824
But he's seriously late.

22:57.542 --> 23:01.004
Turn off the lights before you sleep.
I'll come home as soon as I can.

23:20.982 --> 23:23.568
I NEED TO TELL YOU SOMETHING
I'LL STAY UP AND WAIT

23:25.403 --> 23:26.571
No.

23:27.656 --> 23:29.032
He'll be back soon anyway.

23:54.266 --> 23:55.851
When is he coming?

23:55.934 --> 23:58.019
"I'll come home as soon as I can."

23:58.103 --> 23:59.437
You said, "As soon as I can"!

24:29.134 --> 24:30.177
Did I wake you?

24:34.806 --> 24:36.183
Mr. Mechoori.

24:36.892 --> 24:38.310
What took you so long?

24:39.519 --> 24:41.354
I told you I'd be home late.

24:41.438 --> 24:43.148
Why were you sleeping here?

24:43.231 --> 24:44.357
Did you take your meds?

24:44.441 --> 24:46.735
You only took one pack, right?

24:46.818 --> 24:48.528
Did you have dinner…

25:45.293 --> 25:46.628
I'll head inside for a bit.

26:06.356 --> 26:09.901
Why did I do that? Why?

26:11.695 --> 26:13.571
Why did I even say that?

26:20.328 --> 26:22.414
She's not picking up.

26:22.497 --> 26:24.165
Are you sure Ms. Dam is here?

26:24.249 --> 26:25.375
She said she's in Deokpung,

26:25.458 --> 26:27.669
but when I asked where,
she couldn't answer.

26:27.752 --> 26:29.129
Why?

26:29.212 --> 26:31.089
-Why do you think?
-I know!

26:31.172 --> 26:32.674
-Mr. Proper.
-I'm sure of it.

26:32.757 --> 26:35.468
-Of course. But Ms. Eom, did you hear?
-What?

26:35.552 --> 26:38.179
Mr. Seo said L'Étoile wouldn't do
the follow-up broadcast

26:38.847 --> 26:40.390
unless Ms. Dam does it.

26:41.224 --> 26:42.058
For real?

26:42.142 --> 26:44.477
That's why I'm rooting for Mr. Seo.

26:44.561 --> 26:46.187
And he buys us delicious snacks.

26:46.271 --> 26:47.105
Right. He does.

26:47.188 --> 26:48.189
The person you are…

26:48.273 --> 26:49.482
She's not picking up!

26:49.566 --> 26:51.151
Damn it.

26:51.234 --> 26:52.235
DEOKPUNG FESTIVAL

26:52.319 --> 26:53.486
DEOKPUNG ELEMENTARY SCHOOL

26:55.905 --> 26:57.157
DEOKPUNG COMMUNITY CENTER

26:57.240 --> 26:58.241
Could she be…

26:59.034 --> 27:00.452
This must be the place.

27:05.749 --> 27:08.835
Gosh, the weather's so nice.

27:08.918 --> 27:11.379
But why do you look so down?

27:11.463 --> 27:13.381
Did something happen last night?

27:14.257 --> 27:15.508
No.

27:15.592 --> 27:17.052
Of course not.

27:20.805 --> 27:21.931
Mechoori.

27:23.516 --> 27:24.351
I'm not joining.

27:25.769 --> 27:27.520
-Let's move our things.
-Okay.

27:29.647 --> 27:31.816
-Let's go.
-Right.

27:50.335 --> 27:51.753
How have you been, Mr. Lee?

27:51.836 --> 27:53.338
What brings you here?

27:54.005 --> 27:56.716
I believe our two companies
are no longer involved with each other.

27:56.800 --> 27:58.760
I'm here to meet Ms. Dam.

27:58.843 --> 27:59.928
I heard she's staying here.

28:00.011 --> 28:01.513
Then, you'll know why she's here too.

28:01.596 --> 28:02.555
Don't worry.

28:02.639 --> 28:05.266
Ms. Dam will be back on air soon.

28:06.393 --> 28:08.645
La Fin Essence
isn't L'Étoile's only product.

28:11.815 --> 28:15.443
Do you really think
that would help Ms. Dam?

28:15.527 --> 28:17.654
It would be better than staying here.

28:22.200 --> 28:23.493
We have to use that to…

28:25.495 --> 28:26.955
Ms. Dam.

28:27.038 --> 28:28.039
Mr. Seo.

28:29.374 --> 28:31.126
What brings you here?

28:31.209 --> 28:33.086
I wanted to tell you something.

28:33.169 --> 28:34.421
Can you spare some time?

28:34.504 --> 28:36.047
What's this about?

28:36.131 --> 28:37.549
You can talk inside.

28:38.174 --> 28:40.135
Today's the day we settle this.

28:40.218 --> 28:42.178
We're having a community festival.

28:42.262 --> 28:44.013
Our village has lost ten years straight,

28:44.097 --> 28:46.391
so we're desperate for young competitors.

28:47.517 --> 28:50.395
I believe we need your help.
Could you please help us out?

28:52.439 --> 28:54.232
Would I be of any help though?

28:54.315 --> 28:55.984
Anyone under the age of 40 is an athlete.

29:01.948 --> 29:02.782
Then…

29:03.867 --> 29:04.909
Let's go.

29:05.618 --> 29:07.245
-Really? You're joining us?
-Sure.

29:07.328 --> 29:08.413
Let's go!

29:08.496 --> 29:10.373
-Let's talk after.
-Okay.

29:14.085 --> 29:15.837
What? Hey, Mechoori.

29:15.920 --> 29:17.130
Hurry up!

29:17.213 --> 29:18.381
MARKET STALLS THIS WAY

29:18.465 --> 29:19.466
Hey, Mechoori.

29:21.384 --> 29:23.845
Mechoori! You're really coming?

29:34.272 --> 29:36.149
Goodness, Dam Ye-jin.

29:37.484 --> 29:39.110
This is why she wasn't picking up.

29:41.279 --> 29:45.074
Are you Team Mr. Proper or Team Mr. Seo?

29:45.825 --> 29:46.826
Me?

29:48.453 --> 29:49.496
I'm Team Dam Ye-jin.

29:50.079 --> 29:51.164
Dam…

29:54.793 --> 29:56.419
Then, I'm Team Dam Ye-jin too!

29:56.961 --> 29:58.671
That was a great line.

29:59.380 --> 30:00.840
Have some coffee, everyone.

30:00.924 --> 30:01.925
-Thank you.
-Thank you.

30:02.008 --> 30:04.594
-Hey, can you taste this for me?
-Sure.

30:04.677 --> 30:07.722
Hey, bring some more kimchi
so we can have them cut.

30:07.806 --> 30:11.059
Sure thing! I'll go.

30:11.726 --> 30:12.560
Hey!

30:15.021 --> 30:17.816
Deokpung Village 1!

30:19.901 --> 30:21.569
DEOKPUNG VILLAGE 2

30:21.653 --> 30:23.363
-Let's go!
-Let's go!

30:32.330 --> 30:33.456
-Let's go!
-Let's go!

30:33.540 --> 30:34.999
DEOKPUNG FOOD STALL

30:35.083 --> 30:37.961
-Sweetie, come with us.
-Yes, ma'am.

30:38.044 --> 30:39.295
Let's go, Jong-il!

30:39.379 --> 30:41.631
-Let's go.
-Let's hurry!

30:50.807 --> 30:54.519
Thanks for coming, Ms. Okpo.
It must've been tough.

30:54.602 --> 30:56.312
It's fine.

30:56.396 --> 31:02.151
Making the trip to Deokpung Village 1
isn't difficult at all.

31:02.235 --> 31:06.865
I hear the winning village
gets a TV this year.

31:06.948 --> 31:09.075
Oh, dear! My goodness!

31:09.784 --> 31:12.871
Two years ago, we got a fridge.

31:12.954 --> 31:14.330
-With two doors!
-With two doors!

31:14.414 --> 31:16.541
And last year, we got a tractor.

31:16.624 --> 31:18.167
-Vroom!
-Vroom!

31:18.251 --> 31:20.670
If we win the TV as well this year,

31:21.254 --> 31:25.466
when will Deokpung Village 1
ever get their chance?

31:27.552 --> 31:29.053
It's fine!

31:29.137 --> 31:32.140
Even without those prizes,

31:32.223 --> 31:35.018
-we're doing quite fine.
-Since when?

31:35.101 --> 31:39.105
-Sparkle, sparkle.
-Sparkle, sparkle.

32:17.685 --> 32:20.688
This is practically cheating!

32:20.772 --> 32:22.690
Well, for your village,

32:22.774 --> 32:24.734
-you have Gi-bok, don't you?
-Right.

32:24.817 --> 32:26.152
Gi-bok is…

32:27.070 --> 32:29.906
-very healthy.
-Very healthy.

32:47.173 --> 32:48.508
-Get back in here.
-Yes, ma'am.

32:51.803 --> 32:53.680
Deokpung Village 2!

32:53.763 --> 32:55.723
-Let's go!
-Let's go!

32:55.807 --> 32:57.600
Deokpung Village 1!

32:57.684 --> 33:00.603
-Let's go!
-Let's go!

33:00.687 --> 33:02.855
Mic check. Can you hear me in the back?

33:02.939 --> 33:04.482
-Can you hear me?
-We can hear you!

33:04.565 --> 33:06.150
You can hear me? Okay, then.

33:06.234 --> 33:08.277
-Hello, everyone!
-Hello!

33:08.361 --> 33:14.242
I'm Deokpung Village 1's
lovable village chief, Jeon Won-taek!

33:15.326 --> 33:17.704
Nice to see you all!

33:17.787 --> 33:19.372
All right!

33:19.455 --> 33:21.249
The weather's great today, isn't it?

33:21.332 --> 33:22.208
-Yes!
-Yes!

33:22.291 --> 33:26.713
I'm thrilled that Deokpung Village 1

33:26.796 --> 33:30.133
and our dear neighbors,
Deokpung Village 2,

33:30.216 --> 33:35.430
are gathered here
on this great day to hold this festival.

33:36.889 --> 33:39.058
-You must be pretty close.
-Yes.

33:39.684 --> 33:45.314
Let's put aside
all our concerns and worries

33:45.398 --> 33:47.817
and just enjoy this day!

33:50.319 --> 33:52.030
-By all means…
-Geez.

33:52.113 --> 33:53.406
I hope today

33:54.073 --> 33:55.074
will continue to…

33:55.158 --> 33:57.452
Not only is he educated,
he's long-winded too…

33:58.036 --> 33:59.579
-Yeah!
-Yes.

33:59.662 --> 34:04.584
For 10, 20, 30 years to come,

34:04.667 --> 34:06.294
let us all combine our strength…

34:07.170 --> 34:08.504
Ta-da!

34:08.588 --> 34:09.839
All right. This time,

34:09.922 --> 34:14.761
we'll be deciding
who has the strongest arms in our village.

34:14.844 --> 34:17.472
Anyone who feels pretty strong
within their village

34:17.555 --> 34:19.474
can step up and answer the challenge.

34:19.557 --> 34:21.350
Come on out!

34:22.226 --> 34:23.227
Come on, let's go!

34:27.273 --> 34:29.275
Bow to greet each other.

34:30.068 --> 34:31.402
All right. Let's grab hands.

34:32.403 --> 34:34.197
Hold on tight.

34:36.032 --> 34:36.866
He's tough!

34:36.949 --> 34:39.368
Kwang-mo, I don't want to hurt your pride,

34:39.452 --> 34:41.454
so I'll wait five seconds before winning.

34:41.537 --> 34:43.122
Forget it. Just do your best.

34:43.206 --> 34:44.040
Don't be afraid.

34:44.123 --> 34:45.249
Hold on tight.

34:45.333 --> 34:46.876
Ready, set, go!

34:48.169 --> 34:49.087
You can do it!

34:50.296 --> 34:54.175
You can do it!

35:00.723 --> 35:01.557
More!

35:11.442 --> 35:14.153
Mr. Park, you can do it!

35:15.363 --> 35:19.075
Ms. Eom, I don't think I can do this…

35:19.951 --> 35:21.494
You can do it!

35:22.245 --> 35:24.705
I think I'm going to lose.

35:24.789 --> 35:26.457
I'm sorry.

35:42.515 --> 35:44.308
He's winning!

35:48.104 --> 35:49.313
Park Kwang-mo wins!

36:07.665 --> 36:09.208
Park Kwang-mo!

36:09.292 --> 36:11.627
-Park Kwang-mo!
-Park Kwang-mo!

36:12.211 --> 36:13.713
-Park Kwang-mo!
-Park Kwang-mo!

36:14.672 --> 36:15.673
Park Kwang-mo!

36:15.756 --> 36:17.175
VILLAGE 1 VS VILLAGE 2
1 : 0

36:17.258 --> 36:18.134
WOMEN'S ARM WRESTLING

36:18.217 --> 36:20.219
Gi-sun, let's go!

36:20.845 --> 36:22.180
Let's go!

36:24.599 --> 36:25.808
Kwang-mo,

36:25.892 --> 36:28.394
don't you know she's a reserve athlete
for the Asian Games?

36:28.477 --> 36:30.688
Her opponent's going to get crushed.

36:30.771 --> 36:32.481
No one from Deokpung Village 1?

36:33.691 --> 36:34.692
No one?

36:42.033 --> 36:43.492
Where are you going?

36:43.576 --> 36:45.244
Ms. Eom, you can't.

36:45.328 --> 36:47.413
She's a monster!
She's literally a reserve athlete.

36:49.457 --> 36:51.167
It's okay, Mr. Park.

36:51.834 --> 36:54.045
-No, don't!
-Don't…

36:54.128 --> 36:55.838
-Let's do this!
-You can't!

36:58.382 --> 37:00.760
Bow to greet each other!

37:00.843 --> 37:03.429
Okay, let's grab hands.

37:05.389 --> 37:07.225
-Go easy on her, Gi-sun.
-She can't win.

37:07.308 --> 37:09.018
-I can't watch.
-I can't look.

37:09.101 --> 37:13.314
Ready, set, go!

37:13.397 --> 37:16.067
-You can do it.
-You can do it.

37:26.369 --> 37:27.536
She's letting her stay on.

37:27.620 --> 37:29.330
-No way.
-She's going easy on her.

37:35.336 --> 37:37.672
No, wait. She actually has a chance.

37:45.805 --> 37:47.473
Deokpung Village 1 wins!

37:47.556 --> 37:48.891
I win!

37:55.856 --> 37:57.858
Yeah! I won!

38:01.070 --> 38:04.657
-We won!
-We won!

38:10.288 --> 38:12.164
Ae-ra, aren't I heavy?

38:12.248 --> 38:13.249
Shut your mouth.

38:15.876 --> 38:16.961
DISINFECTANT

38:19.964 --> 38:23.009
Ae-ra, I'm usually good at fighting--

38:23.092 --> 38:24.135
Shut your mouth.

38:29.932 --> 38:32.226
This really was the first time!
I've never done it before!

38:32.310 --> 38:34.395
Jong-yeon convinced me to try it
and I was curious.

38:34.478 --> 38:36.647
I promise not to smoke again.
Ae-ra, forgive me!

38:36.731 --> 38:39.608
Ae-ra, please let it slide just this once!

38:39.692 --> 38:40.943
Shut your mouth!

38:41.027 --> 38:43.863
You were smoking
because your stupid mouth is always open!

38:43.946 --> 38:46.115
I swear I won't.
Please forgive me just this once!

38:46.198 --> 38:47.616
-What's wrong with you?
-Please!

38:47.700 --> 38:52.496
It's because I'm worried about you!
What's gotten into you?

38:57.793 --> 38:58.627
Yeah!

39:01.505 --> 39:03.507
But this feeling's supposed to be
for Moon Ae-ra.

39:18.147 --> 39:19.690
Ae-ra…

39:35.998 --> 39:37.541
Why do I feel okay?

39:41.879 --> 39:43.047
I feel so calm.

39:45.091 --> 39:47.635
This next game is charades.

39:47.718 --> 39:48.844
Where were you from?

39:48.928 --> 39:50.096
-Okay, teams.
-I'm from Seoul.

39:50.179 --> 39:53.933
Please select your players now.

39:54.016 --> 39:55.351
Let's hurry and…

39:55.434 --> 39:56.602
Deokpung Village 1! What are…

39:56.685 --> 39:59.021
Come on, Deokpung Village 1! Focus!

39:59.105 --> 40:00.898
Hey, Jong-il! Stop eating rice puffs…

40:00.981 --> 40:03.109
All right, already. Give it a rest.

40:03.192 --> 40:06.070
Okay, who's going to do charades?

40:10.533 --> 40:12.034
Everyone's waiting.

40:12.785 --> 40:14.537
Stop eating, will you?

40:14.620 --> 40:15.996
Hurry up and come out.

40:18.582 --> 40:20.709
What's your name?

40:21.544 --> 40:23.212
Hello, ma'am. My name is Eric.

40:23.879 --> 40:24.713
"Eregi"?

40:26.507 --> 40:28.092
Yes, Eregi.

40:28.926 --> 40:29.802
Eregi.

40:30.761 --> 40:32.721
Eregi, come with me.

40:33.806 --> 40:35.182
What? Where are we going, ma'am?

40:38.060 --> 40:39.854
VILLAGE 1 VS VILLAGE 2
2 : 2

40:39.937 --> 40:41.814
CHARADES

40:42.982 --> 40:45.109
I don't know if that blonde
even knows Korean.

40:45.192 --> 40:47.862
Ready, set, go!

40:47.945 --> 40:49.572
TOO MANY COOKS SPOIL THE BROTH

40:55.286 --> 40:57.538
Eregi, just try anything.

40:57.621 --> 40:59.206
It's fine.

41:07.673 --> 41:10.092
Too many cooks spoil the broth!

41:10.176 --> 41:11.427
Correct!

41:15.764 --> 41:17.099
FALLING ON DEAF EARS

41:23.981 --> 41:26.817
-Falling on deaf ears!
-Correct!

41:26.901 --> 41:28.569
AS THE TWIG IS BENT, SO GROWS THE TREE

41:30.446 --> 41:31.697
As the twig is bent,

41:31.780 --> 41:34.492
-so grows the tree!
-Correct!

41:35.409 --> 41:37.161
He's crying.

41:37.244 --> 41:39.747
Crying over spilled milk!

41:39.830 --> 41:41.373
Correct!

41:42.791 --> 41:43.918
All right!

41:46.462 --> 41:47.463
What's that?

41:47.546 --> 41:50.216
EVERYONE LOOKS OUT FOR THEIR OWN SKIN,
BUT FEW RISK IT FOR OTHERS

41:53.344 --> 41:54.178
What is it?

41:55.179 --> 41:56.430
Just give it a try.

41:59.600 --> 42:02.603
Everyone looks out for their own skin,

42:02.686 --> 42:05.731
but few will risk it for someone else!

42:10.945 --> 42:14.782
Correct! Deokpung Village 1,
one minute and 35 seconds!

42:24.208 --> 42:25.793
Eregi, I can't believe this!

42:52.152 --> 42:54.071
Mechoori is our village genius.

42:54.154 --> 42:55.322
VILLAGE 1 VS VILLAGE 2
3 : 2

42:55.406 --> 42:57.157
-He's a genius.
-Of course.

42:57.241 --> 43:00.619
We're going to win this game for sure.

43:02.454 --> 43:04.206
Okay, get ready.

43:04.290 --> 43:05.958
-Get set.
-Let's go.

43:06.041 --> 43:07.209
Go!

43:07.293 --> 43:08.586
LET SLEEPING DOGS LIE

43:13.632 --> 43:15.259
Yeah, that's right!

43:17.344 --> 43:18.429
Sleep…

43:21.140 --> 43:22.516
And kiss?

43:22.600 --> 43:23.559
I missed you.

43:28.397 --> 43:31.567
Mechoori, why aren't you guessing?

43:32.901 --> 43:34.737
If you don't know, just skip it!

43:34.820 --> 43:36.488
-No, don't skip!
-It's okay.

43:36.572 --> 43:38.073
Pass!

43:40.451 --> 43:41.869
Pass!

43:41.952 --> 43:43.203
AT A LOSS FOR WORDS

43:46.790 --> 43:51.503
AT A LOSS FOR WORDS

43:51.587 --> 43:53.380
KISS

43:58.636 --> 43:59.511
Pass!

44:01.013 --> 44:03.015
All right, it's okay. No, it's not okay!

44:03.098 --> 44:04.475
Look, he's just getting started.

44:04.558 --> 44:05.851
Just watch.

44:06.769 --> 44:07.895
LIE THROUGH ONE'S TEETH

44:12.941 --> 44:15.027
Just say something!

44:16.987 --> 44:17.988
Pass!

44:18.072 --> 44:19.573
Mr. Mechoori!

44:20.616 --> 44:21.992
What are you doing?

44:22.618 --> 44:24.995
-This is so frustrating!
-Mechoori!

44:25.079 --> 44:26.455
We're going to lose!

44:28.999 --> 44:29.958
Your…

44:34.213 --> 44:35.047
Lips…

44:37.716 --> 44:38.550
Love…

44:52.898 --> 44:53.857
I love your lips!

44:53.941 --> 44:55.526
KIND WORDS BRING KIND RESPONSES

44:55.609 --> 44:59.446
I LOVE YOUR LIPS!

45:11.583 --> 45:12.960
Wrong!

45:13.836 --> 45:15.879
Deokpung Village 1, time's up!

45:17.423 --> 45:19.258
Hey, you fool!

45:31.228 --> 45:32.062
Mr. Mechoori…

45:33.063 --> 45:33.897
Goodness…

45:34.731 --> 45:36.108
I'm sorry.

45:36.817 --> 45:37.818
I'm really sorry!

45:40.988 --> 45:42.781
-So what was it?
-What?

45:42.865 --> 45:44.408
What was the lips thing?

45:44.950 --> 45:46.368
What about you and Mr. Park?

45:47.536 --> 45:48.829
What's going on with you two?

45:49.580 --> 45:51.457
Am I being left out again?

45:52.541 --> 45:54.710
SOM'S VARIETY SHOP

45:54.793 --> 45:58.505
I'm sure it'll take ages for you
to dry your hair

45:58.589 --> 46:00.966
with that weak dryer you have at home.

46:01.049 --> 46:03.343
Well, as for this hair dryer,

46:03.427 --> 46:06.054
it's completely different
from those weak ones.

46:06.138 --> 46:10.184
It's designed to be low-noise,
you don't have to worry about waking up

46:10.267 --> 46:11.351
your family at night.

46:11.435 --> 46:13.520
Won't it use a lot of electricity?

46:13.604 --> 46:15.689
There's no need to worry about that!

46:15.772 --> 46:17.524
It has the highest energy
efficiency rating,

46:17.608 --> 46:19.651
so using it 30 minutes a day
for a month will add

46:19.735 --> 46:21.445
only a few thousand won more to your bill.

46:21.528 --> 46:23.906
But it's so small.
I bet the air flow's not that great.

46:23.989 --> 46:25.908
There's no need to explain.
Feel it yourself.

46:26.492 --> 46:28.160
Doesn't it feel so nice… Oh, gosh!

46:28.243 --> 46:29.495
-Hey!
-Sorry!

46:29.578 --> 46:31.997
-Geez…
-Goodness.

46:33.665 --> 46:35.375
Anyways, I don't need it.

46:35.459 --> 46:37.127
Come on, sir.

46:37.211 --> 46:39.379
If you apply warm air
to your scalp regularly,

46:39.463 --> 46:42.090
it'll boost blood flow
and keep your mind sharp.

46:42.174 --> 46:44.801
It's perfect for helping you
stay warm in winter.

46:44.885 --> 46:46.637
And you know you have to dry your toes

46:46.720 --> 46:49.556
after showering
to prevent athlete's foot, right?

46:49.640 --> 46:52.518
This can help you from head to toe.

46:52.601 --> 46:53.727
And you still don't need it?

46:55.479 --> 46:56.730
How much is it again?

46:56.813 --> 46:59.233
Only 49,000 won.

46:59.316 --> 47:01.527
-I want one too!
-Me too!

47:01.610 --> 47:02.486
Please line up.

47:02.569 --> 47:04.488
-Line up, please!
-Hey, get in line!

47:06.907 --> 47:08.700
I thought I was watching you, Ms. Dam.

47:08.784 --> 47:10.869
I know, right?
There was a mini Dam Ye-jin here.

47:15.415 --> 47:16.416
Hang on.

47:21.505 --> 47:22.839
Som-yi.

47:24.466 --> 47:25.968
Here, drink this.

47:30.055 --> 47:32.224
I'll cover you. Drink up.

47:46.280 --> 47:47.364
VILLAGE 1 VS VILLAGE 2
3 : 3

47:47.447 --> 47:48.657
Ta-da!

47:50.075 --> 47:53.245
Look at this, everyone.
It's three to three right now.

47:53.328 --> 47:57.666
Okay, it's time for the last game
to decide the winner.

47:57.749 --> 48:01.837
Let us begin the highlight
of the festival, the relay race.

48:01.920 --> 48:04.965
Deokpung Village 2!

48:18.645 --> 48:21.773
Let's go, Deokpung Village 2!

48:26.737 --> 48:27.571
Thank you.

48:34.119 --> 48:35.579
Don't push yourself too hard.

48:42.753 --> 48:44.463
Okay, runners.

48:44.546 --> 48:47.049
Please take your place
at the starting line.

48:47.132 --> 48:47.966
Good luck, Mr. Seo.

48:54.348 --> 48:55.641
-Jin-yi.
-Yeah?

48:55.724 --> 48:56.725
Let's change our order.

48:58.352 --> 48:59.394
Sure.

49:03.482 --> 49:07.194
Ready, set, go!

49:11.239 --> 49:12.783
You're doing great!

49:23.460 --> 49:24.294
Just a bit more!

49:24.378 --> 49:25.837
Let's go! Come on!

49:33.136 --> 49:34.262
There you go! A bit more!

49:43.313 --> 49:44.356
Mechoori!

49:48.652 --> 49:51.071
Matthew! Yes! Go!

49:52.114 --> 49:53.240
All the way!

49:55.784 --> 49:56.618
Mechoori!

50:25.230 --> 50:26.565
-Mechoori!
-No, no!

50:26.648 --> 50:28.358
-What is he doing?
-Pass the baton!

50:28.442 --> 50:29.776
Why is he still running?

50:29.860 --> 50:31.111
What…

50:31.194 --> 50:32.112
Hey!

50:41.037 --> 50:43.915
He should be disqualified!
He ran half a lap more!

50:43.999 --> 50:45.500
I mean, it can happen!

50:45.584 --> 50:47.252
It happens! It's fine!

50:47.335 --> 50:50.297
-No, it can't! He should be disqualified!
-It's not like that!

50:51.298 --> 50:53.008
Okay, all right!

50:53.091 --> 50:53.925
He's disqualified!

50:57.554 --> 50:58.722
Mr. Park!

51:00.056 --> 51:01.516
Mr. Park! Oh, no!

51:02.559 --> 51:03.810
Mr. Park!

51:21.453 --> 51:24.122
DEOKPUNG VILLAGE 2 HAS ALREADY WON

51:24.206 --> 51:26.833
DEOKPUNG VILLAGE 1

51:33.965 --> 51:35.342
Can I call you?

51:42.057 --> 51:43.058
Well…

51:46.228 --> 51:47.062
Okay.

51:57.906 --> 51:59.074
I have something to tell you.

52:00.158 --> 52:01.159
Do you have a minute?

52:04.663 --> 52:06.414
It's going to take a while to clean up.

52:06.498 --> 52:07.874
-How about tomorrow?
-No, tonight.

52:10.460 --> 52:11.461
It has to be tonight.

52:17.008 --> 52:18.844
All right. Let's go and talk.

52:26.226 --> 52:27.602
You're not cold?

52:27.686 --> 52:29.729
No, I'm okay.

52:33.525 --> 52:34.734
Geez!

52:34.818 --> 52:35.861
What the heck?

52:35.944 --> 52:37.320
Let me talk to you.

52:42.033 --> 52:43.076
You know,

52:43.577 --> 52:45.495
I came here
because I was worried about you.

52:45.579 --> 52:47.247
Geez, why would you worry about me?

52:49.958 --> 52:53.920
You know 70% of your body
is made up of work.

52:54.546 --> 52:57.299
But that condition for survival
just disappeared,

52:58.091 --> 52:59.926
so I didn't know if you'd make it or not.

53:00.802 --> 53:03.346
I brought all of these for you. See?

53:08.685 --> 53:09.853
Give them to me then.

53:11.730 --> 53:13.481
You didn't seem to need them.

53:17.611 --> 53:18.695
You look well, Ye-jin.

53:19.779 --> 53:21.031
You finally look human.

53:27.370 --> 53:28.371
Ms. Eom.

53:28.455 --> 53:30.957
Then, for the drive on the way back…

53:31.041 --> 53:32.500
-Thank you.
-I'll do it.

53:33.293 --> 53:34.711
We'll head back now, Ms. Dam.

53:34.794 --> 53:37.172
Okay. I'll be back after I get some rest.

53:38.632 --> 53:41.217
But don't rest for too long, okay?

53:41.301 --> 53:42.844
Without you, our team is like…

53:42.928 --> 53:45.472
-A hot dog without the sausage.
-That's it. Got that?

53:45.555 --> 53:47.223
-Go on, now.
-Bye.

53:47.307 --> 53:49.517
-Drive safely.
-We'll get going. Bye!

53:49.601 --> 53:51.978
-Make sure to eat well.
-Okay.

54:02.072 --> 54:04.074
It seems you're busy here as well.

54:07.410 --> 54:08.954
Could you spare some time for me now?

54:16.544 --> 54:18.588
I heard from Ms. Yang earlier

54:19.965 --> 54:22.509
that you collapsed the day you came here.

54:26.763 --> 54:27.764
I'm sorry.

54:29.057 --> 54:31.017
I wanted to apologize to you in person.

54:31.768 --> 54:33.228
Come on.

54:33.311 --> 54:34.896
What happened with HIT

54:34.980 --> 54:36.898
was just a result of my decision.

54:37.565 --> 54:39.901
It's nothing for you to apologize about.

54:39.985 --> 54:42.737
Still, if you hadn't become involved
with L'Étoile,

54:42.821 --> 54:44.823
you wouldn't be here right now.

54:48.702 --> 54:50.912
I wanted to come earlier,

54:51.705 --> 54:54.082
but I didn't want to apologize
with empty words,

54:54.165 --> 54:55.834
so it took a while.

54:58.044 --> 54:59.254
Ms. Dam,

55:01.589 --> 55:02.966
come back to Seoul with me.

55:08.638 --> 55:11.099
We're doing another QA test
for La Fin Essence

55:11.182 --> 55:12.809
and a follow-up broadcast afterwards.

55:13.518 --> 55:16.438
We're discussing launching
other L'Étoile products on HIT as well.

55:16.521 --> 55:18.648
-Mr. Seo, I--
-Ms. Dam.

55:19.315 --> 55:21.568
Allow me to help so you can go back

55:22.777 --> 55:24.195
to the work that you love to do.

55:25.196 --> 55:26.948
Come with me, Ms. Dam.

55:37.208 --> 55:41.796
DEOKPUNG RESTING SPOT

55:42.881 --> 55:44.966
Aren't you curious about what I'll say?

55:48.303 --> 55:50.680
I guess you already know
what I'm going to say.

55:51.890 --> 55:53.808
But I know everything too.

55:55.602 --> 55:58.104
I know you're already aware of my feelings

55:58.730 --> 56:00.648
and that you've been playing dumb.

56:01.983 --> 56:04.778
Still, I wanted to tell you this myself.

56:07.989 --> 56:11.409
Thanks to you, I got to live
in a warm neighborhood

56:12.452 --> 56:15.163
and learned how to share
care and affection with others.

56:15.246 --> 56:18.208
I feel like I've grown roots here now.

56:18.291 --> 56:19.125
So thank you.

56:22.128 --> 56:24.798
And along with that gratitude,

56:25.381 --> 56:26.841
I've grown to like you too.

56:28.343 --> 56:29.719
How do you feel about me?

56:36.351 --> 56:37.519
What are you doing?

56:38.186 --> 56:40.021
You're supposed to tell me to get a grip.

56:40.688 --> 56:41.981
Because I'm Som-yi's sister.

56:47.445 --> 56:48.488
Jin-yi.

56:49.155 --> 56:51.908
-I--
-Gosh, you're so frustrating.

56:54.911 --> 56:56.663
I'm sorry, Jin-yi.

56:57.247 --> 56:58.414
Did you know

56:59.457 --> 57:01.167
you were looking at Dam Ye-jin all day?

57:02.877 --> 57:05.088
Don't make excuses for your own feelings.

57:05.171 --> 57:07.549
You saw what just happened to me, right?

57:09.467 --> 57:10.510
Bye.

57:10.593 --> 57:13.179
I feel embarrassed,
so wait three minutes and leave.

57:27.861 --> 57:29.612
Thank you, Mr. Seo.

57:30.447 --> 57:31.281
But…

57:32.282 --> 57:34.409
You don't have to put in
so much effort to help me.

57:34.492 --> 57:37.787
I know you can return without my help.

57:38.413 --> 57:41.749
I just don't want you
to waste too much time here--

57:41.833 --> 57:43.460
Sung-mi said I looked well.

57:46.087 --> 57:47.922
I've never been told that before.

57:50.175 --> 57:51.468
These days,

57:52.260 --> 57:55.722
I feel like I'm walking a path
that I used to run through.

57:57.849 --> 58:00.518
I never realized how long an hour was

58:00.602 --> 58:02.937
even though I'd do live shows
for two hours every day.

58:04.397 --> 58:05.482
Are you sure you're okay?

58:06.524 --> 58:07.692
I really am okay.

58:09.402 --> 58:11.571
I think I need this time.

58:12.530 --> 58:15.241
So don't feel guilty about me.

58:15.992 --> 58:18.286
The one who should
actually apologize to me

58:18.369 --> 58:19.329
is myself.

58:21.539 --> 58:22.373
Still…

58:24.042 --> 58:27.378
feel free to tell me
whenever you need my help.

58:31.090 --> 58:31.925
I'm…

58:33.718 --> 58:35.929
waiting for you, Ms. Dam.

58:39.849 --> 58:41.434
I'm good at waiting

58:42.477 --> 58:43.978
even though I don't enjoy it.

59:53.715 --> 59:56.759
Korea really is far away.

01:00:00.597 --> 01:00:02.765
L'ETOILE
EXECUTIVE DIRECTOR SEO ERIC

01:00:11.733 --> 01:00:12.942
What are you doing out here?

01:00:14.569 --> 01:00:16.529
You must have talked for quite a while.

01:00:24.954 --> 01:00:26.456
PAIN RELIEF SPRAY

01:00:29.167 --> 01:00:31.127
Were you late because of this?

01:00:31.210 --> 01:00:33.588
Apply that before bed.
And go to the hospital tomorrow.

01:00:36.883 --> 01:00:38.134
Let's go inside.

01:00:41.262 --> 01:00:42.555
Sit down.

01:00:43.222 --> 01:00:44.766
We have a lot to talk about.

01:01:06.996 --> 01:01:08.456
My nickname is Fact Check.

01:01:08.539 --> 01:01:11.459
So let me check a few things.

01:01:12.502 --> 01:01:13.336
Okay.

01:01:14.045 --> 01:01:16.589
In that relay race earlier,

01:01:16.673 --> 01:01:17.590
why did you do that?

01:01:19.342 --> 01:01:20.927
You hurt your ankle yesterday.

01:01:27.684 --> 01:01:29.310
And those…

01:01:29.394 --> 01:01:30.353
Those corner guards.

01:01:30.436 --> 01:01:32.271
Why did you install them?

01:01:33.856 --> 01:01:34.857
It's in case

01:01:35.441 --> 01:01:36.567
you get hurt.

01:01:39.487 --> 01:01:41.072
Why did you make that daily schedule?

01:01:42.198 --> 01:01:43.491
Why did you say

01:01:43.574 --> 01:01:45.952
you'd give me one pack of pills a day?

01:01:46.035 --> 01:01:47.704
Why did you bring me here?

01:01:47.787 --> 01:01:50.373
Why are you so nice to me?

01:01:58.089 --> 01:01:59.966
Are these questions difficult to answer?

01:02:06.764 --> 01:02:07.765
That day…

01:02:08.725 --> 01:02:09.726
Why did you do it?

01:02:10.601 --> 01:02:12.979
What? What day?

01:02:15.690 --> 01:02:18.776
The day you kissed me.

01:02:27.785 --> 01:02:29.287
Is that question difficult to answer?

01:02:32.999 --> 01:02:34.041
No, I…

01:02:40.339 --> 01:02:43.593
I didn't take the medicine
that you left that day.

01:02:45.178 --> 01:02:47.597
I was waiting to talk to you
when you came back.

01:02:48.931 --> 01:02:50.850
But when I heard you coming,

01:02:50.933 --> 01:02:53.895
my heart started pounding,
and I pretended to be asleep.

01:02:55.188 --> 01:02:58.357
I was wondering when I should act
as if I'd just been woken up.

01:02:58.441 --> 01:03:02.361
But you kept doing stuff for me
so I could sleep well,

01:03:02.445 --> 01:03:04.739
so I couldn't open my eyes.

01:03:06.157 --> 01:03:09.619
My heart was pounding so loudly
that they were ringing in my ears.

01:03:09.702 --> 01:03:11.579
Do you know how worried I was

01:03:11.662 --> 01:03:13.498
that you'd hear it too?

01:03:21.464 --> 01:03:22.799
You were pretending to be asleep?

01:03:22.882 --> 01:03:23.883
Yes!

01:03:25.635 --> 01:03:28.346
I did it because I was nervous.

01:03:30.515 --> 01:03:33.017
-What?
-You still haven't answered my question.

01:03:34.310 --> 01:03:35.436
What was the question?

01:03:39.440 --> 01:03:41.234
Why did you pretend not to remember?

01:03:42.777 --> 01:03:44.278
I don't think that was the question.

01:03:46.489 --> 01:03:48.908
I pretended not to remember
because of you.

01:03:48.991 --> 01:03:52.245
You're the one who first acted
like nothing happened.

01:03:52.328 --> 01:03:53.204
And that's not all.

01:03:53.287 --> 01:03:55.289
You freaked out
even when our arms touched.

01:03:55.373 --> 01:03:57.083
You took Changsik and ran off without me.

01:03:57.667 --> 01:03:59.585
How could I say anything to you?

01:04:05.132 --> 01:04:06.300
What's that look?

01:04:06.384 --> 01:04:07.969
Do I look like a fool to you right now?

01:04:08.928 --> 01:04:10.721
I'm Dam Ye-jin!

01:04:10.805 --> 01:04:14.934
I'm not someone
who usually rambles on like this!

01:04:17.395 --> 01:04:19.480
This is all because of you, Mr. Mechoori.

01:04:22.775 --> 01:04:23.609
Then, this…

01:04:27.321 --> 01:04:28.823
is because of you, Ms. Dam.

01:05:54.575 --> 01:05:56.577
SOLD OUT ON YOU

01:06:29.694 --> 01:06:31.529
What did you two do last night?

01:06:32.571 --> 01:06:35.408
I think I first fell for you
when I saw you like this.

01:06:35.491 --> 01:06:36.993
You talk to yourself too loudly.

01:06:37.076 --> 01:06:38.327
I said that for you to hear.

01:06:38.411 --> 01:06:40.329
They can't get enough of each other!

01:06:40.413 --> 01:06:44.000
Mechoori! It's Som-yi!
What am I going to do?

01:06:44.083 --> 01:06:46.711
Why on earth
did you bring that woman here?

01:06:46.794 --> 01:06:49.964
What happened to Som-yi was my fault.

01:06:50.047 --> 01:06:52.091
I've put everything
on the line for Ms. Dam.

01:06:52.174 --> 01:06:54.051
But is this the best you can do for her?

01:06:54.135 --> 01:06:56.971
Ms. Dam. There's something
I need to tell you.

01:07:05.938 --> 01:07:07.940
Subtitle translation by Juyoung Park
